  "name": "HyperScale | Scalability Engine",
  "alias": null,
  "accountGrade": 6.8,
  "description": "Engagement scope for HyperScale | Scalability Engine: migrate the remaining on-premise services to a managed cloud platform and modernise the surrounding delivery tooling.\n\nPhase 1 covers discovery and dependency mapping across the existing estate, including a documented inventory of services, data stores, scheduled jobs and third-party integrations. Phase 2 covers the lift-and-shift of stateless services behind a load balancer, with blue/green cutover and rollback runbooks. Phase 3 covers data migration with dual-write verification, followed by decommissioning of the legacy hosts.\n\nOut of scope: application rewrites, schema redesign, and any change to the existing authentication provider. Success is measured by cutover completed with no unplanned downtime beyond the agreed maintenance window, and by p95 latency remaining within 10% of the pre-migration baseline.",
